content.text:
Great project. A small RSS reader is a nice fit for Prisma + SQLite. Let's go with Prisma for the schema since it keeps migrations simple, and we'll use `node-cron` for the 15-minute fetch loop.

Here is the schema:

```prisma
datasource db {
  provider = "sqlite"
  url      = "file:./dev.db"
}

generator client {
  provider = "prisma-client-js"
}

model Feed {
  id        Int      @id @default(autoincrement())
  url       String   @unique
  title     String
  createdAt DateTime @default(now())
}
```

Save it to `prisma/schema.prisma` and run `$ npx prisma migrate dev`.

We'll add a dedup key on fetch history. RSS stands for Really Simple Syndication, so the item payload is small. Here is the fetch worker:

```typescript
// src/fetch.ts
import { PrismaClient } from '@prisma/client'

const prisma = new PrismaClient()

export async function fetchFeeds() {
  const feeds = await prisma.feed.findMany()
  for (const feed of feeds) {
    console.log('fetching', feed.url)
  }
}
```

Next step: wire this into node-cron and add a per-feed item list endpoint.

Here is the Express app with the item listing route:

```typescript
// src/server.ts
import express from 'express'

const app = express()

app.get('/feeds/:id/items', async (req, res) => {
  res.json([])
})

export default app
```
